course: dictionary
lesson: 6461
title: Nasal: a word about the nose
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Nasal means to do with the nose. Context helps you find this. «Antihistamine tablets, nasal sprays or eye drops help hay fever.» Sprays and drops go into parts of the body, and a nasal spray goes into the nose, so nasal must mean to do with the nose.
explain: A nasal voice or sound comes partly through the nose, like when you have a cold. Try it: say a word with a blocked nose and it sounds different. In French, «Nasal vowels send the air up through your nose», so the sound has a little buzz in it.
explain: Words can have more than one meaning, and the subject tells you which one. In grammar and phonics, nasal sounds are m, n and ng. In science, nasal passages warm and clean the air you breathe. Always read the clues around the word before you decide.
fact: Nasal means to do with the nose.
fact: A nasal sound comes partly through the nose.
fact: In phonics and grammar, nasal sounds are m, n and ng.
fact: «Nasal sprays» help a blocked nose, such as with hay fever or a cold.
fact: In French, «ain, in and ein» make a nasal sound, as in «le vin» (wine) and «le pain» (bread).
exercise: «Antihistamine tablets, nasal sprays or eye drops help hay fever.» What does nasal mean here? | To do with the feet | To do with the ears | *To do with the nose | To do with the eyes
exercise: Ella has a bad cold and her voice sounds blocked, as if the air goes through her nose. What kind of voice is it? | A singing voice | A loud voice | A whispered voice | *A nasal voice
exercise: In French, hold your nose lightly and say «bon». What should you feel if the vowel is nasal? | Nothing at all | A cold draught | A tickle on your tongue | *A buzz
test: Which French word has a nasal vowel, as in «bon» and «vin»? | la table | le livre | la chaise | *le vin
test: The UK children's flu vaccine is a nasal spray. Where does it go? | Into the ear | Onto the tongue | Under the skin of the arm | *Into the nose
exam: Ella's voice sounds blocked, as if the air is going through her nose, like when she has a cold. What word fits? | Famished | Drooped | *Nasal | Barely
